{"c":[{"id":"73cd22e0cad86c6d","sum":"B29/D2-06: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen; choice questions go only to askChoices consumers. Page presses are hand-offs; only a goalAccept with its digest runs goal steps, never taskControl; goal targets are Target.exact.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1c75543de1b1c0e8","sum":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen (before and after fill's Jev calls): add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading. Questions with choices go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; others read AskRefused's sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2ff420afa6ce639a","text":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen, checked before and after the fill's Jev calls; three reviews each found something fill reads that the record missed, so add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-c755285b7eff0669","text":"B29: Ask questions with choices (planner/choices.ts) go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; AskAsks extends AskRefused, so any other caller reads the old refusal sentence.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf5de0df55b6d70e","sum":"D2-06: 'Continue' stays unclassified; the one goal press is e:reveal on a whole 'Next'; page presses are hand-offs. Only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs goal steps; a goal task is never resumed by taskControl; goal targets are Target.exact.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1712f90f65a11b14","text":"D2-06: 'Continue' is deliberately unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive macOS dialogs); the one goal press capability is e:reveal on a whole 'Next' (goals/capabilities.ts). Page presses are always hand-offs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1ba2dff3c7f2e7e3","text":"D2-06: only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs a goal's steps; a goal task (GoalRuns.owns) is never resumed by taskControl, and a pause stops it. Goal targets are Target.exact (key+role, a button's label): resolveLocally never falls back for them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"046b14781a65d0ff","sum":"D2-06/B30: GoalRuns.blocked must return null once a segment ends, or undo is refused; a goal host's plan Ask comes back as AskGoal. Keep name patterns case-sensitive; goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc/Subject, and To takes only the answered message's From.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"24a976c12b8a54f1","sum":"D2-06/B30: GoalRuns.blocked (inside Helper.authorize) must return null once a segment ends, or undo is refused. A goal host's Ask with route plan comes back as AskGoal (planAsk goals:true) for helper.offerGoal; other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105431Z-2d9978b4db29946e","text":"D2-06: GoalRuns.blocked runs inside Helper.authorize before every act; it must return null once a segment ends, or a goal task's undo (undoBlocked -> authorize) is refused.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-9e86109ce30422ae","text":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan is offered as a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true returns AskGoal; helper.offerGoal); other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode. planAsk overloads: goals absent/false types as AskDraft.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b7329c13cd423b17","sum":"B30: keep name patterns case-sensitive (the i flag folds \\p{Lu}). Goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject; To takes only the From of the message the reply answers, rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf); D2-06 scenes need mailWindow line 0 to be From.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-b6135cb945f89335","text":"B30: JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to match lower case too; a case-insensitive name pattern let 'Thanks, I'll pay' skip Jev. Keep name patterns case-sensitive.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-c27c662d572bf540","text":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject, and To takes only the From address in the header block of the message the reply window answers (Re: <subject>), rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf). D2-06 scenes rely on mailWindow line 0 being its From header.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
